Notebook[
 {Cell["Complete ten-component corrected-dualization source certificate", 
   "Title"], 
  Cell["Exact in rotation, generic unequal charges, first order in \
alphaPrime", "Subtitle"], Cell["Scope", "Section"], 
  Cell["This self-contained notebook differentiates the torsion-free \
four-derivative scalar with respect to all ten independent components of the \
upper-index five-dimensional three-form. Components that vanish on the BMPV \
background are substituted only after differentiation. The notebook does not \
read a desired third gauge potential and does not use closure as a fitting \
condition. It also checks the dualization sign implied by the final \
Lagrange-multiplier term +C wedge (d h+F wedge G), the physical lower \
Levi--Civita tensor, and the positive Eq. (4.1) third potential.", "Text"], Cell["Dualization convention", 
  "Section"], Cell["Convention equation. The flat-index symbol has epsilonLower[0,1,2,3,4]=+1 and epsilonUpper[0,1,2,3,4]=-1; the curved epsilonLower used in the duality contraction is its five-vielbein transform and includes the determinant. With A3=+H0^(-1) Theta, the final action gives h=-(1/2) Exp[2 Phi] epsilonCurvedLower contracted with F3Upper+(alphaPrime/8) J. The alphaPrime source keeps a plus sign. On the static background, Exp[2 Phi] star5 F3 has component -q0 Sin[theta]/4, whereas h has +q0 Sin[theta]/4. The executable ledger requires the minus branch to pass and the plus branch to fail.", "Text"], Cell["Normalization and invariant completion", 
   "Section"], Cell["An executable variation of the fully contracted \
two-derivative kinetic term proves that differentiation with respect to one \
independent antisymmetric component gives minus the corresponding lower-index \
component. Hence the independently differentiated four-derivative source \
enters the dualization equation directly, with no extra division by 3!. The \
notebook then projects all ten equatorial derivatives onto the complete \
stationary SU(2)-invariant three-form basis. This projection fixes the \
off-equator sin(theta) factors and the relation J_(t r phi)=cos(theta) J_(t r \
psi).", "Text"], Cell["Complete machine calculation", "Section"], 
  Cell[BoxData["(* Independent rotating corrected-dualization calculation.\n  \
 Scratch source only; the final human artifact is a self-contained notebook. \
*)\n\nClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n$HistoryLength = 0;\n$Assumptions = r > 0 && \
qp > 0 && qm > 0 && q0 > 0 && 0 < th < Pi && Element[a, Reals];\ncoords = {t, \
r, th, ph, ps}; n = Length[coords];\nIf[Environment[\"BMPV_NUMERIC_CHARGES\"] \
=== \"1\", qp = 5; qm = 3; q0 = 7];\nIf[StringQ[Environment[\"BMPV_A\"]] && \
StringLength[Environment[\"BMPV_A\"]] > 0,\n  a = \
ToExpression[Environment[\"BMPV_A\"]]];\nhp = 1 + qp/r^2; hm = 1 + qm/r^2; h0 \
= 1 + q0/r^2;\nw = a/(2 r^2);\n\n(* Mostly-plus five-dimensional string-frame \
BMPV metric. *)\ng = ConstantArray[0, {n, n}];\ng[[1, 1]] = -1/(hp \
hm);\ng[[2, 2]] = h0;\ng[[3, 3]] = h0 r^2/4;\ng[[4, 4]] = h0 r^2/4 (Sin[th]^2 \
+ Cos[th]^2) - w^2 Cos[th]^2/(hp hm);\ng[[5, 5]] = h0 r^2/4 - w^2/(hp \
hm);\ng[[4, 5]] = g[[5, 4]] = h0 r^2 Cos[th]/4 - w^2 Cos[th]/(hp hm);\ng[[1, \
4]] = g[[4, 1]] = -w Cos[th]/(hp hm);\ng[[1, 5]] = g[[5, 1]] = -w/(hp \
hm);\ngi = FullSimplify[Inverse[g], Assumptions -> r > 0 && h0 > 0 && hp > 0 \
&& hm > 0];\n\nchrist = Table[1/2 Sum[gi[[aa, dd]] (D[g[[dd, bb]], \
coords[[cc]]] + D[g[[dd, cc]], coords[[bb]]] - D[g[[bb, cc]], coords[[dd]]]), \
{dd, n}], {aa, n}, {bb, n}, {cc, n}];\nriemUComp[aa_, bb_, cc_, dd_] := \
riemUComp[aa, bb, cc, dd] = FullSimplify[D[christ[[aa, bb, dd]], \
coords[[cc]]] - D[christ[[aa, bb, cc]], coords[[dd]]] + Sum[christ[[aa, cc, \
ee]] christ[[ee, bb, dd]] - christ[[aa, dd, ee]] christ[[ee, bb, cc]], {ee, \
n}]];\nriemDComp[aa_, bb_, cc_, dd_] := riemDComp[aa, bb, cc, dd] = \
FullSimplify[Sum[g[[aa, ee]] riemUComp[ee, bb, cc, dd], {ee, \
n}]];\nPrint[\"STAGE_CONNECTION_DONE\"];\n\ntheta = {1, 0, 0, w Cos[th], \
w};\nA = theta/hp; B = -theta/hm;\ntwoForm[pot_] := Table[D[pot[[jj]], \
coords[[ii]]] - D[pot[[ii]], coords[[jj]]], {ii, n}, {jj, n}];\nraise2[x_] := \
Table[FullSimplify[Sum[gi[[i, p]] gi[[j, q]] x[[p, q]], {p, n}, {q, n}]], {i, \
n}, {j, n}];\nf = twoForm[A]; gg = twoForm[B];\nsigma = 1/2 Log[hp/hm]; \
varphi = 1/4 Log[h0^2/(hp hm)];\nfm = FullSimplify[Exp[sigma] f - Exp[-sigma] \
gg];\nfp = FullSimplify[Exp[sigma] f + Exp[-sigma] gg];\nds = Table[D[sigma, \
coords[[ii]]], {ii, n}];\ndsU = FullSimplify[gi.ds];\n\n(* All ten \
independent upper-index components must be varied.  Components\n   that \
vanish on the BMPV background are set to zero only after\n   differentiation; \
L4 contains terms linear in h, so omitting them as\n   variables would not \
certify their derivatives. *)\ntriples = Subsets[Range[n], {3}];\nhv = \
Array[hh, Length[triples]];\nhU[i_, j_, k_] := Module[{s = Signature[{i, j, \
k}], key = Sort[{i, j, k}], pos}, If[s == 0, 0, pos = FirstPosition[triples, \
key]; If[MissingQ[pos], 0, s hv[[First[pos]]]]]];\nhEntries = \
Select[(Append[#, hU @@ #] &) /@ Tuples[Range[n], 3], Last[#] =!= 0 &];\nhD = \
Table[Sum[g[[i, p]] g[[j, q]] g[[k, s]] hU[p, q, s], {p, n}, {q, n}, {s, n}], \
{i, n}, {j, n}, {k, n}];\n\n(* The horizontal reduced three-form is not \
purely magnetic when rotating. The six-dimensional bridge gives\n   \
h0 = -M_het - G_old wedge A = q0 sigma123/4\n     \
+ (hp hm)^(-1) dOmega wedge Theta.\n   The final Lagrange-multiplier sign \
therefore gives h0 = -Exp[2 varphi] star5 d(theta/h0). *)\nhBridgeMagneticComp[i_, j_, k_] := \
If[Sort[{i, j, k}] === {3, 4, 5}, Signature[{i, j, k}] (q0 Sin[th]/4), \
0];\nh0DComp[i_, j_, k_] := h0DComp[i, j, k] = FullSimplify[hBridgeMagneticComp[i, j, k] \
- (gg[[i, j]] A[[k]] + gg[[j, k]] A[[i]] + gg[[k, i]] \
A[[j]])];\nh0UComp[i_, j_, k_] \
:= h0UComp[i, j, k] = FullSimplify[Sum[gi[[i, p]] gi[[j, q]] gi[[k, s]] \
h0DComp[p, q, s], {p, n}, {q, n}, {s, n}]];\nhRules = Table[hv[[u]] -> \
h0UComp @@ triples[[u]], {u, Length[triples]}];\n(* Executable \
independent-component normalization check.  This derives, rather\n   than \
assumes, the permutation multiplicity of the kinetic term. *)\nkineticL = \
-1/12 Sum[hD[[i, j, kk]] hU[i, j, kk],\n  {i, n}, {j, n}, {kk, \
n}];\nkineticVariationResiduals = Table[Factor[Cancel[Together[\n   \
(D[kineticL, hv[[u]]] + hD[[Sequence @@ triples[[u]]]]) /. hRules]]],\n  {u, \
Length[triples]}];\nkineticVariationPass = And @@ (PossibleZeroQ /@ \
kineticVariationResiduals);\nPrint[\"KINETIC_INDEPENDENT_COMPONENT_RESIDUALS=\
\", \
InputForm[kineticVariationResiduals]];\nPrint[\"KINETIC_INDEPENDENT_COMPONENT\
_PASS=\", kineticVariationPass];\ndetg = \
FullSimplify[Det[g]];\n(* This chart reverses the physical orientation. *)\nepsD[idx_List] := -Signature[idx] Sqrt[-detg];\nc0 = \
theta/h0; hc0D = twoForm[c0]; hc0U = raise2[hc0D];\ndualH0DComp[i_, j_, k_] \
:= FullSimplify[1/2 Sum[epsD[{i, j, k, mu, nu}] hc0U[[mu, nu]], {mu, n}, {nu, \
n}]];\nleadingDualPlusPass = And @@ (TrueQ[FullSimplify[h0DComp @@ # == Exp[2 \
varphi] dualH0DComp @@ #]] & /@ triples);\nleadingDualMinusPass = And @@ \
(TrueQ[FullSimplify[h0DComp @@ # == -Exp[2 varphi] dualH0DComp @@ #]] & /@ \
triples);\nPrint[\"LEADING_DUAL_PLUS_PASS=\", leadingDualPlusPass, \"; \
MINUS_PASS=\", \
leadingDualMinusPass];\nfinalActionDualitySignPass = TrueQ[leadingDualMinusPass && !leadingDualPlusPass];\nPrint[\"FINAL_ACTION_MINUS_DUALITY_PASS=\", finalActionDualitySignPass];\nPrint[\"STAGE_BACKGROUND_DONE\"];\n\nfmU = \
raise2[fm]; fpU = raise2[fp];\nfmMixed = Table[FullSimplify[Sum[gi[[j, q]] \
fm[[i, q]], {q, n}]], {i, n}, {j, n}];\nfpMixed = \
Table[FullSimplify[Sum[gi[[j, q]] fp[[i, q]], {q, n}]], {i, n}, {j, \
n}];\n\n(* Contraction helpers. h2DD_{mn}=h_{m rho lambda} h_n^{rho lambda}. \
*)\nh1D2U[mu_, rr_, ss_] := Sum[gi[[rr, p]] gi[[ss, q]] hD[[mu, p, q]], {p, \
n}, {q, n}];\nh2U1D[mu_, nu_, rr_] := Sum[g[[rr, s]] hU[mu, nu, s], {s, \
n}];\nh2D1U[mu_, nu_, rr_] := Sum[gi[[rr, s]] hD[[mu, nu, s]], {s, n}];\nh2DD \
= Table[Sum[hD[[mu, rr, ss]] h1D2U[nu, rr, ss], {rr, n}, {ss, n}], {mu, n}, \
{nu, n}];\nh2UU = Table[Sum[gi[[mu, p]] gi[[nu, q]] h2DD[[p, q]], {p, n}, {q, \
n}], {mu, n}, {nu, n}];\nh2scalar = Sum[h2DD[[mu, nu]] h2UU[[mu, nu]], {mu, \
n}, {nu, n}];\nh4 = Sum[hD[[aa, bb, rr]] h2D1U[cc, dd, rr] hU[aa, cc, ss] \
h2U1D[bb, dd, ss], {aa, n}, {bb, n}, {cc, n}, {dd, n}, {rr, n}, {ss, \
n}];\n\nfm2DD = Table[Sum[fm[[mu, rr]] fmMixed[[nu, rr]], {rr, n}], {mu, n}, \
{nu, n}];\nfp2DD = Table[Sum[fp[[mu, rr]] fpMixed[[nu, rr]], {rr, n}], {mu, \
n}, {nu, n}];\nPrint[\"STAGE_CONTRACTIONS_DONE\"];\n\n(* Only the h-dependent \
terms of L4 in Eq. (4derlag3). *)\nl4QuarticH = -1/8 h2scalar + 1/24 \
h4;\nl4Rh2 = -1/2 Sum[riemDComp[e1[[1]], e1[[2]], e2[[1]], e2[[2]]]\n  \
e1[[4]] e2[[4]] g[[e1[[3]], e2[[3]]]],\n  {e1, hEntries}, {e2, \
hEntries}];\nl4QuadraticMatter =\n +1/16 Sum[hU[aa, bb, rr] hU[cc, dd, ss] \
g[[rr, ss]] fm[[aa, bb]] fm[[cc, dd]], {aa, n}, {bb, n}, {cc, n}, {dd, n}, \
{rr, n}, {ss, n}]\n +1/8 Sum[hU[aa, bb, rr] hU[cc, dd, ss] g[[rr, ss]] \
fm[[aa, cc]] fm[[bb, dd]], {aa, n}, {bb, n}, {cc, n}, {dd, n}, {rr, n}, {ss, \
n}]\n -1/4 Sum[h2UU[[mu, nu]] fm2DD[[mu, nu]], {mu, n}, {nu, n}]\n \
-Sum[h2UU[[mu, nu]] ds[[mu]] ds[[nu]], {mu, n}, {nu, n}]\n -1/4 Sum[h2UU[[mu, \
nu]] fp2DD[[mu, nu]], {mu, n}, {nu, n}]\n -1/16 Sum[hU[aa, bb, rr] hU[cc, dd, \
ss] g[[rr, ss]] fp[[aa, bb]] fp[[cc, dd]], {aa, n}, {bb, n}, {cc, n}, {dd, \
n}, {rr, n}, {ss, n}]\n +1/8 Sum[hU[aa, bb, rr] hU[cc, dd, ss] g[[rr, ss]] \
fp[[aa, cc]] fp[[bb, dd]], {aa, n}, {bb, n}, {cc, n}, {dd, n}, {rr, n}, {ss, \
n}];\nl4LinearMatter =\n +1/2 Sum[hU[aa, bb, cc] fp[[aa, dd]] fm[[bb, cc]] \
dsU[[dd]], {aa, n}, {bb, n}, {cc, n}, {dd, n}]\n +1/2 Sum[hU[aa, bb, cc] \
fm[[aa, dd]] fp[[bb, cc]] dsU[[dd]], {aa, n}, {bb, n}, {cc, n}, {dd, n}]\n \
-Sum[hU[aa, bb, cc] fp[[aa, dd]] Sum[gi[[dd, ee]] fm[[cc, ee]], {ee, n}] \
ds[[bb]], {aa, n}, {bb, n}, {cc, n}, {dd, n}];\nl4h = l4QuarticH + l4Rh2 + \
l4QuadraticMatter + l4LinearMatter;\nPrint[\"STAGE_L4_BUILT\"];\n\nkraw = \
Table[Factor[Cancel[Together[(D[l4h, hv[[u]]] /. hRules /. th -> Pi/2)]]], \
{u, Length[triples]}];\nsectorLagrangians = <|\"QuarticH\" -> l4QuarticH, \
\"Rh2\" -> l4Rh2,\n  \"QuadraticMatter\" -> l4QuadraticMatter,\n  \
\"LinearMatter\" -> l4LinearMatter|>;\nkrawSectors = \
AssociationMap[Function[key, With[{sector = sectorLagrangians[key]},\n  \
Table[Factor[Cancel[Together[\n    (D[sector, hv[[u]]] /. hRules /. th -> \
Pi/2)]]],\n    {u, Length[triples]}]]], \
Keys[sectorLagrangians]];\nsectorSumPass = And @@ (PossibleZeroQ /@ \
Flatten[Table[\n  kraw[[u]] - Total[(#[[u]] &) /@ Values[krawSectors]],\n  \
{u, Length[triples]}]]);\n(* Regression for the delivered monolithic \
notebook.  Its fresh-kernel static\n   output was -5 q0^3/(q0+r^2)^3, exactly \
the QuarticH member.  The separately\n   evaluated source below proves that \
this old output omitted the nonzero Rh2\n   member.  Keeping this executable \
comparison prevents a future return to\n   the evaluation-order-sensitive \
monolithic assignment. *)\nlegacyMonolithicStatic345 = -5 q0^3/(q0 + \
r^2)^3;\nquarticStatic345 = Factor[Cancel[Together[\n  \
krawSectors[\"QuarticH\"][[10]] /. a -> 0]]];\nrh2Static345 = \
Factor[Cancel[Together[\n  krawSectors[\"Rh2\"][[10]] /. a -> \
0]]];\nfullStatic345 = Factor[Cancel[Together[kraw[[10]] /. a -> \
0]]];\nlegacyEqualsQuarticStaticPass = PossibleZeroQ[\n  \
legacyMonolithicStatic345 - quarticStatic345];\nrh2StaticNonzeroPass = \
!PossibleZeroQ[rh2Static345];\nfullStaticDiffersFromLegacyPass = \
!PossibleZeroQ[\n  fullStatic345 - \
legacyMonolithicStatic345];\nfullStaticSectorSumPass = \
PossibleZeroQ[fullStatic345 -\n  Total[(Factor[Cancel[Together[#[[10]] /. a \
-> 0]]] &) /@\n    Values[krawSectors]]];\nequatorDerivative = \
AssociationThread[triples, kraw];\ninvariantCoefficientA = \
equatorDerivative[{3, 4, 5}];\ninvariantCoefficientB = equatorDerivative[{1, \
3, 4}];\ninvariantCoefficientC = equatorDerivative[{1, 2, 5}];\n(* The most \
general stationary SU(2)-invariant three-form in this sector is\n     A(r) \
sin(th) dth^dph^dps\n   + B(r) sin(th) dt^dth^dph\n   + C(r) \
dt^dr^(dps+cos(th)dph).\n   This fixes the off-equator completion and, in \
particular, J124=cos(th)J125. *)\ninvariantCompletion = \
AssociationThread[triples, Table[Switch[triples[[u]],\n   {3, 4, 5}, \
invariantCoefficientA Sin[th],\n   {1, 3, 4}, invariantCoefficientB \
Sin[th],\n   {1, 2, 5}, invariantCoefficientC,\n   {1, 2, 4}, \
invariantCoefficientC Cos[th],\n   _, 0], {u, \
Length[triples]}]];\nequatorProjectionResiduals = \
Table[Factor[Cancel[Together[\n   (invariantCompletion[triples[[u]]] /. th -> \
Pi/2) - kraw[[u]]]]],\n  {u, Length[triples]}];\nequatorProjectionPass = And \
@@ (PossibleZeroQ /@ equatorProjectionResiduals);\nequatorZeroCount = \
Count[kraw, x_ /; PossibleZeroQ[x]];\nequatorNonzeroCount = Length[kraw] - \
equatorZeroCount;\nledger = <|\n  \"FinalActionMinusDualityWithPositiveA3\" -> \
finalActionDualitySignPass,\n  \"AllTenIndependentComponentsVaried\" -> \
(Length[triples] == 10),\n  \"KineticIndependentComponentVariation\" -> \
kineticVariationPass,\n  \"FourSectorSum\" -> sectorSumPass,\n  \
\"DeliveredMonolithicStaticEqualsQuarticOnly\" ->\n    \
legacyEqualsQuarticStaticPass,\n  \"Rh2StaticMemberIsNonzero\" -> \
rh2StaticNonzeroPass,\n  \"FullStaticDiffersFromDeliveredMonolithic\" ->\n    \
fullStaticDiffersFromLegacyPass,\n  \"FullStaticFourSectorSum\" -> \
fullStaticSectorSumPass,\n  \"EquatorDerivativeZeroCountSeven\" -> \
(equatorZeroCount == 7),\n  \"EquatorDerivativeNonzeroCountThree\" -> \
(equatorNonzeroCount == 3),\n  \"InvariantBasisProjection\" -> \
equatorProjectionPass,\n  \"OffEquator124EqualsCosTheta125\" -> \
PossibleZeroQ[\n    invariantCompletion[{1, 2, 4}] - Cos[th] \
invariantCompletion[{1, 2, 5}]]\n  |>;\nfinalPass = And @@ \
Values[ledger];\nPrint[\"ALL_TEN_DERIVATIVES=\", InputForm[Thread[triples -> \
kraw]]];\nPrint[\"ALL_TEN_DERIVATIVES_BY_SECTOR=\", \
InputForm[krawSectors]];\nPrint[\"SECTOR_SUM_PASS=\", \
sectorSumPass];\nPrint[\"STATIC_MONOLITHIC_REGRESSION=\", InputForm[<|\n  \
\"DeliveredMonolithic\" -> legacyMonolithicStatic345,\n  \"QuarticH\" -> \
quarticStatic345, \"Rh2\" -> rh2Static345,\n  \"Full\" -> fullStatic345,\n  \
\"DeliveredEqualsQuartic\" -> legacyEqualsQuarticStaticPass,\n  \
\"Rh2Nonzero\" -> rh2StaticNonzeroPass,\n  \"FullDiffersFromDelivered\" -> \
fullStaticDiffersFromLegacyPass,\n  \"FullSectorSum\" -> \
fullStaticSectorSumPass|>]];\nPrint[\"ADDITIONAL_BACKGROUND_ZERO_COMPONENT_DE\
RIVATIVES=\", InputForm[\n  Select[Thread[triples -> kraw], \
!MemberQ[{{3,4,5},{1,3,4},{1,2,5},{1,2,4}}, First[#]] && Last[#] =!= 0 \
&]]];\nPrint[\"INVARIANT_COMPLETION=\", \
InputForm[invariantCompletion]];\nPrint[\"EQUATOR_ZERO_COUNT=\", \
equatorZeroCount, \"; NONZERO_COUNT=\", \
equatorNonzeroCount];\nPrint[\"LEDGER=\", \
InputForm[ledger]];\nPrint[\"FINAL_PASS=\", finalPass];\nPrint[\"K_NONZERO=\
\", Select[Thread[triples -> kraw], Last[#] =!= 0 &]];"], "Input"]}, 
 WindowSize -> {1400, 900}, StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"]
